@prefix backlog: <http://example.org/backlog#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix lc: <http://example.org/fixture-lineage-completeness#> .

# Proves LineageCompletenessShape's register-wide "no Objective anywhere" and "no
# ScopeStatement anywhere" clauses (v1.24.0, owner's ruling 2026-10-09: closing
# backlog_clause_proof's never-proven-clause backlog).
#
# These two clauses are FILTER NOT EXISTS over the WHOLE merged graph, not over
# anything scoped to $this -- so they can only be proven by an ISOLATED fixture file
# that contains no backlog:Objective and no backlog:ScopeStatement anywhere at all.
# fixture_negative_v1_24_0.ttl cannot prove them: it already carries both types in
# service of dozens of other shapes' own fixtures. Per reference_abox(), validating
# this file alone strips the live register's own namespace content before merging,
# so this file's own emptiness is what the query actually sees.
#
# A bare register with one real, non-archived Lineage: the v1.121.0 waiver
# ("waived when every lineage that exists is archived") only applies once every
# lineage is archived, so this active lineage keeps both clauses live rather than
# waived.
lc:Bl_Bare a backlog:Backlog .
lc:Lin_Active a backlog:Lineage ; backlog:lineageArchived false .

lc:Bl_Bare backlog:hasExpectedPolarity backlog:Polarity_Negative .
